# P1 round 2: a resume continues on the provider the session recorded,
# whatever the profile says by then. fx goes vercel -> codex and xfx gateway
# -> llmux, as provider-carry does; after the exit the profile is written back
# as it was at launch, on the Gateway (`reseed`), so the resume has the
# session's record against the profile's. fx's resume puts back the
# recorded provider and model (restoreRuntimePreferences,
# app_session_runtime.zig:6147); the turn after it goes to codex / llmux,
# carrying both turns.
fx: seed provider-carry-fx.json
xfx: seed provider-carry-xfx.json
fx: homefile .fx/chatgpt-auth.json provider-carry-chatgpt-auth.json
fx: env FX_E2E_OPENAI_CODEX_MODELS_URL=http://127.0.0.1:@PORT@/codex/models FX_E2E_OPENAI_CODEX_RESPONSES_URL=http://127.0.0.1:@PORT@/codex/responses
nomodel
gateway provider-carry-turns.json
work provider-carry-ws
wait 6
snap start
type read the notes and tell me what they say
key Enter
wait 15
snap turn1
type /provider
key Enter
wait 4
key Down
wait 1
key Enter
wait 10
snap switched
type what day was it again?
key Enter
wait 15
snap turn2
keep
type /quit
key Enter
wait 4
home quit
fx: reseed provider-carry-fx.json
xfx: reseed provider-carry-xfx.json
home reseeded
fx: relaunch --resume-last
xfx: relaunch --resume last
wait 10
snap resumed
type and after the resume?
key Enter
wait 15
snap turn3
home end
gwlog
type /quit
key Enter
wait 3
